      "objective": "Elect core as the current root, use west/core as a root port and east/west as Alternate, with the west-to-east tree path through core. Keep every supplied bridge, port and link online/up. Priorities and costs may vary when these explicit results still hold.",
      "difficulty": "Beginner",
      "minutes": 20,
      "steps": [
        "Inspect the supplied graph",
        "Apply bridge and port configuration",
        "Check current root, roles and tree path"
      ],
      "guide": [],
      "explanation": "The desired root wins by composite bridge identity. Each nonroot adds its local rootward port cost. The alternate port stays operational but discards in this ideal steady state. Physical availability is an explicit requirement.",
      "hints": [
        "Compare bridge priority before MAC.",
        "Do not disable another bridge or link to win an election.",
        "A current tree path must use links where both ends forward."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/support/docs/lan-switching/spanning-tree-protocol/24062-146.html"
